# Aspire AppHost layout and resource names

Lire `.cursor/rules/neox-rules.json` pour `{rootNamespace}`, `{solutionSlug}`.

This repository ships **Neox Aspire packages**. It is not a product runtime. Aspire AppHosts here are **isolated sample/test harnesses** under `tests/` (for example `tests/efcore-migration-worker/*/apphost`, `tests/auth-providers/sample-apphost`, `tests/azure-custom-domains/sample-apphost`). They are not the saas **test AppHost** (`saas/tests/aspire`) and not the Events delivery AppHost.

There is no single `{paths.appHost}` / `{paths.serviceDefaults}` for the repo. Layout is **relative to each harness**: `apphost/` and `service-defaults/` beside that harness’s tests.

## ServiceNames

Un fichier `service-defaults/ServiceNames.cs` **par harness**. Classes imbriquées = segment kebab après `{Prefix}`. Interpolated strings : `Prefix` + préfixe de groupe privé.

`Prefix` is **per harness** (for example `neox-efmw-sql`), not `{solutionSlug}`.

```csharp
public static class ServiceNames
{
    public const string Prefix = "neox-efmw-sql";

    public static class Services
    {
        public const string Gateway = $"{ServicesPrefix}-gateway";
        public const string Migrations = $"{ServicesPrefix}-migrations";
        public const string {PascalSlug} = $"{ServicesPrefix}-{slug}";
        private const string ServicesPrefix = $"{Prefix}-services";
    }
}
```

| Groupe | Pattern |
|--------|---------|
| `Infrastructure` | `{Prefix}-infra-{slug}` or `{Prefix}-infrastructure-{slug}` |
| `Databases` | `{Prefix}-databases-{slug}` |
| `Services` | `{Prefix}-services-{slug}` (`gateway`, `migrations`, métier de test) |
| `Workers` | `{Prefix}-{slug}` when the harness uses a workers group (migration services) |
| `Web` | `{Prefix}-web-{slug}` |

Tout `{Prefix}-services-*` vit dans `Services` — pas de classes `Gateway` / `MigrationServices`. Do not add a repo-wide `{aspire.resources}` map; each harness owns its ids.

Do not add resource constants until a resource exists.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — product solutionSlug or Events AppHost ids
builder.AddProject<...>("aspire-web-app");
public const string App = "events-web-app";
```

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — harness Prefix
builder.AddProject<...>(ServiceNames.Workers.Migration);
```

## AppHost — un fichier par groupe

`apphost/Program.cs` : `CreateBuilder` → `X.Configure(builder)` → `Build().Run()` uniquement.

Fichiers seulement si le groupe a des resources : `Infrastructure.cs`, `Databases.cs`, `Migrations.cs`, `Auth.cs`, `Services.cs`, `Gateway.cs`, `Web.cs`.

Empty graph: no group files and no `Configure` calls.

**Configure order:** Infrastructure → Databases → Migrations → Auth → Services → Gateway → Web.

Chaque groupe : `public static class {Group}` + une propriété `IResourceBuilder<T>` par resource (`get; private set; = null!`) + `Configure(...)`.

```csharp
public static class Databases
{
    public static IResourceBuilder<SqlServerDatabaseResource> Application { get; private set; } = null!;

    public static void Configure(IDistributedApplicationBuilder builder)
    {
        Application = Infrastructure.SqlServer.AddDatabase(ServiceNames.Databases.Application, "application");
    }
}
```

Cross-groupe : `Infrastructure.SqlServer`, `Databases.Application`. Ids : `ServiceNames.*`.

**Interdit :** `apphost.cs` à la racine du repo ; resources en propriétés de `Program` ; câbler ces harnesses dans l’AppHost Events ou le test AppHost saas (`saas/tests/aspire`).
